{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QGeometricLanglands.QVonMangoldtFunction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QGeometricLanglands.QVonMangoldtFunction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MaxIdealRq.isFundamental","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MaxIdealRq.isFundamental","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/q-von-mangoldt-function.lean#L54-L54","doc":"Whether this ideal corresponds to a fundamental defect.\n\n**`Bool`, not `Prop`, since 2026-09-07.**  It was a field typed with the\n*universe* `Prop`, so the value carried a proposition and an instance\nchose it.  It is a FLAG, and the commented-out weight below consumes it\nas one (`if m.isFundamental then …`), which needs `Decidable` — free for\n`Bool` and not available for an arbitrary `Prop`.  The `ℝ` sibling in\n`explicit-formula.lean` already declares it `Bool`; this is the two\nagreeing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MaxIdealRq.norm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MaxIdealRq.norm","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/q-von-mangoldt-function.lean#L43-L43","doc":"The norm N(𝔪) — cardinality of the residue field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MaxIdealRq.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MaxIdealRq.mk","kind":"ctor","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/q-von-mangoldt-function.lean#L41-L41","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MaxIdealRq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MaxIdealRq","kind":"structure","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/q-von-mangoldt-function.lean#L29-L54","doc":"A maximal ideal of the coordinate ring, carrying a norm (residue field\ncardinality) and a flag marking fundamental defects.\n\n**Renamed from `MaxIdeal` 2026-09-07.**  `explicit-formula.lean` declares a\n*different* `structure MaxIdeal` — over `ℝ` rather than `R_q` — in **the\nsame namespace** `QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate`.  Two structures of one name in\none namespace is a duplicate declaration; it compiles today only because\nthese are content-block siblings rather than library modules, so nothing\nimports both.  The duplication itself is deliberate and documented (that\nfile's docstring says \"the Laurent `R_q` form lives in the sibling\n`q-von-mangoldt-function`\"); sharing the name was not.  The suffix says\nwhich ground ring this one is over. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.q_inv_param","kind":"def","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/q-von-mangoldt-function.lean#L27-L27","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.q_param","kind":"def","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/q-von-mangoldt-function.lean#L26-L26","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.R_q","kind":"def","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/q-von-mangoldt-function.lean#L25-L25","signatureChunk":0}]}